cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GL1F Forest in research, cite this software record and the accompanying author manuscript."
title: "GL1F Forest: Reconstructible Integer Gradient-Boosted Trees for Exact Local and EVM Inference"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fedorov
    given-names: Mikhail
repository-code: "https://github.com/GenesisL1/Forest"
url: "https://gl1f.com"
version: 0.2.3
date-released: "2026-09-05"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - gradient-boosted decision trees
  - deterministic inference
  - EVM
  - blockchain
  - model serialization
  - reproducible computing
abstract: >-
  GL1F Forest is an open implementation of fixed-depth,
  integer-quantized gradient-boosted decision trees with browser, Python, C++,
  and Solidity execution surfaces. Its canonical public binary representation
  supports independent reconstruction and exact integer replay.
references:
  - type: report
